WEBVTT

00:00:23.465 --> 00:00:24.466
Mr. President.

00:00:24.549 --> 00:00:26.009
I found the TV remote.

00:00:26.093 --> 00:00:27.094
Good work, Sergeant.

00:00:27.177 --> 00:00:29.346
I'm awarding you the Purple Heart.

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:31.014
But I wasn't injured.

00:00:31.598 --> 00:00:32.849
Ow!

00:00:34.184 --> 00:00:35.477
Well, enough governing.

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:37.187
It's Saturday morning, damn it.

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.648
Let's watch some cartoons.

00:00:43.068 --> 00:00:45.112
It's time to fall into...

00:00:45.195 --> 00:00:48.949
the Futurama and Friends
Saturday Morning Fun Pit!

00:00:49.032 --> 00:00:52.244
Here comes Bendee-Boo
and the Mystery Crew!

00:00:53.245 --> 00:00:56.248
Bendee, Bendee-Boo, what's wrong with you?

00:00:56.331 --> 00:00:59.209
You're such a lousy mascot

00:00:59.292 --> 00:01:02.963
No one understands a single word you say

00:01:03.046 --> 00:01:06.133
Not even the jerk in the ascot

00:01:09.594 --> 00:01:12.097
Rite my riny retal rass!

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.898
It sure was nice of your nephew

00:01:21.982 --> 00:01:25.444
to invite us to his cloning lab
here in the Repeating Forest.

00:01:25.527 --> 00:01:28.405
Uh-huh. Hey, like, here's a puzzler.

00:01:28.488 --> 00:01:31.575
How old are we on a scale of 14 to 32?

00:01:33.827 --> 00:01:35.954
Did anyone else hear that weird laugh?

00:01:36.038 --> 00:01:37.289
It's spooky.

00:01:37.372 --> 00:01:40.417
It doesn't seem to correspond
to anything funny happening.

00:01:40.500 --> 00:01:41.501
I'll say.

00:01:47.632 --> 00:01:49.092
Turn around.

00:01:49.176 --> 00:01:50.344
Go away.

00:01:50.427 --> 00:01:52.287
Do it now.

00:01:52.312 --> 00:01:53.371
Rikes!

00:01:53.972 --> 00:01:56.224
Splinkies! What was that?

00:01:56.308 --> 00:01:58.769
I don't know. It's a mystery.

00:01:58.852 --> 00:02:00.937
Like, I've got a bigger mystery.

00:02:01.021 --> 00:02:02.731
How am I going to fill my hungry stomach?

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:08.278
Yeah. Where can we find food
here in the woods?

00:02:08.362 --> 00:02:10.238
How about that kabuki theater?

00:02:10.739 --> 00:02:14.534
Like, where there's a kabuki theater,
there's a concession stand.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.658
Say, Fry, why do you
always have the munchies?

00:02:21.742 --> 00:02:23.827
And also your eyes are bloodshot,
you're paranoid,

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.412
and the van has a skunky odor.

00:02:25.495 --> 00:02:26.705
Search me.

00:02:26.788 --> 00:02:28.290
No, don't. I'm carrying.

00:02:38.550 --> 00:02:41.595
I do enjoy a well-buttered floor.

00:02:42.638 --> 00:02:43.805
George Takei?

00:02:43.889 --> 00:02:45.599
Reorge Rakei?

00:02:45.682 --> 00:02:47.559
Sorry to haunt you so effectively.

00:02:47.643 --> 00:02:51.521
I thought you kids were that Dragon Ghost
that's been spooking the town.

00:02:51.605 --> 00:02:54.232
Like, what's the story with the yakitori?

00:02:54.316 --> 00:02:55.484
Help yourselves.

00:02:55.567 --> 00:02:59.571
But I warn you,
that chicken is over a year old.

00:03:03.659 --> 00:03:07.496
Why is the food in your concession stand
so old, Mr. Takei?

00:03:07.579 --> 00:03:11.375
You see, Amy, this used to be
the most popular kabuki theater

00:03:11.458 --> 00:03:13.543
in the entire outskirts of town.

00:03:13.627 --> 00:03:17.881
But people stopped coming after they built
that darned basketball arena.

00:03:19.508 --> 00:03:22.761
Now everybody likes basketball
instead of kabuki.

00:03:22.844 --> 00:03:25.597
It's an insult to my Japanese heritage.

00:03:25.681 --> 00:03:28.725
How so? This is America, not Japan.

00:03:28.809 --> 00:03:30.727
Maybe so. I'm not sure.

00:03:30.811 --> 00:03:33.438
Now, how many tickets would you like
for the show?

00:03:33.522 --> 00:03:34.523
Like, none.

00:03:34.606 --> 00:03:36.483
But thanks for the yucky-tori.

00:03:39.069 --> 00:03:42.406
Another grave insult to my ancestry.

00:03:52.499 --> 00:03:53.500
Nu?

00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:55.502
Is this the Professor's cloning lab?

00:03:55.585 --> 00:03:58.171
Cloning is a sin against nature!

00:03:58.255 --> 00:04:01.508
But yes.
Follow me to the Professor's cloning room.

00:04:04.553 --> 00:04:06.054
You see, I'm his butler.

00:04:06.138 --> 00:04:10.183
Ah, my uncle Fry
and his mystery-solving friends.

00:04:10.267 --> 00:04:12.519
Perhaps you can make sense of the...

00:04:12.603 --> 00:04:14.980
What is it
that's been haunting us, Zoidberg?

00:04:15.063 --> 00:04:16.064
Ghost.

00:04:17.232 --> 00:04:19.651
Now then, let me show you my lab.

00:04:20.819 --> 00:04:22.654
This is my cloning machine.

00:04:23.071 --> 00:04:26.033
This is where I keep
various lengths of wire.

00:04:26.116 --> 00:04:28.952
And those are the Harlem Globetrotters.

00:04:29.036 --> 00:04:30.954
- The Globetrotters?
- Ruh Robe-rotters?

00:04:31.038 --> 00:04:33.373
What you doin' wearin' an ascot, brother?

00:04:33.457 --> 00:04:35.042
I think it looks nice.

00:04:43.258 --> 00:04:44.593
Whoa, whoa, whoa...

00:04:47.262 --> 00:04:49.598
What are you Globetrotters doing here?

00:04:49.681 --> 00:04:51.475
We're in town for the big game.

00:04:51.558 --> 00:04:53.894
And we stopped by
to help our friend, the Professor,

00:04:53.977 --> 00:04:55.562
with his cloning machine.

00:04:55.646 --> 00:04:58.690
Just call me
the Clone Prince of Basketball.

00:05:05.197 --> 00:05:08.492
Like, it's basketball superstar
Larry Bird!

00:05:08.575 --> 00:05:10.911
Larry Bird, what are you doing here?

00:05:10.994 --> 00:05:13.538
Hi. This is Larry Bird calling.

00:05:13.622 --> 00:05:16.333
Listen, my agent sent me
that cartoon script,

00:05:16.416 --> 00:05:19.836
and I've decided
I don't want to be involved in any way.

00:05:21.004 --> 00:05:23.090
Nice to meet you, Larry Bird.

00:05:23.173 --> 00:05:27.219
Okay, let's clone us
a whole team of Larry Birds.

00:05:33.892 --> 00:05:36.061
Now we can practice for the big game.

00:05:36.144 --> 00:05:38.563
We figure,
if we can beat five Larry Birds,

00:05:38.647 --> 00:05:39.982
we can beat anybody.

00:05:40.065 --> 00:05:42.442
Cloning is wrong. It's wrong, I say!

00:05:42.526 --> 00:05:45.362
Oh, I just hope
that mysterious Dragon Ghost

00:05:45.445 --> 00:05:47.447
doesn't show up at the lab again.

00:05:47.531 --> 00:05:51.118
But why would a ghost wanna stop
the Globetrotters from practising?

00:05:51.201 --> 00:05:53.954
And against a team of clones, no less.

00:05:58.125 --> 00:06:02.629
Well, gang, it looks like we've got
more of the same mystery on our hands.

00:06:16.727 --> 00:06:20.647
Like, the real mystery is how I'm gonna
get any sleep with all this noise.

00:06:20.731 --> 00:06:22.149
I need some air.

00:06:22.983 --> 00:06:26.361
It's me, the Dragon Ghost.

00:06:26.445 --> 00:06:27.529
We met before.

00:06:27.613 --> 00:06:28.947
Like, yikes!

00:06:32.993 --> 00:06:35.537
It's time to spring into action, gang.

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:38.290
Okay...

00:06:38.373 --> 00:06:41.001
Rabbit goes around the tree...

00:06:41.084 --> 00:06:42.336
there.

00:06:42.419 --> 00:06:44.588
All right, it's time to get to the bottom

00:06:44.671 --> 00:06:48.175
of what, at this point,
can only be called a mystery.

00:06:48.258 --> 00:06:49.301
Let's split up.

00:06:49.384 --> 00:06:52.888
Eight of us will stay here
with this dragon trap the Professor built.

00:06:52.971 --> 00:06:56.016
Meanwhile, Fry, Bendee,
you go look for the dragon.

00:06:56.099 --> 00:06:59.728
Like, you guys are terrible friends
for always sending us to our deaths.

00:06:59.811 --> 00:07:00.896
I'm not going.

00:07:00.979 --> 00:07:02.147
Re reither!

00:07:02.230 --> 00:07:04.024
Would you do it for a Bendee Brew?

00:07:04.107 --> 00:07:05.108
Ro-kay.

00:07:05.192 --> 00:07:06.944
Ri'm a ralcoholic.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.784
Yummy, yummy, yummy
I got love in my tummy

00:07:13.867 --> 00:07:16.578
And I feel like a-lovin' you

00:07:17.913 --> 00:07:19.331
Love, you're such a sweet thing

00:07:19.414 --> 00:07:20.958
Good enough to eat thing

00:07:21.041 --> 00:07:23.710
And that's just a-what I'm gonna do

00:07:24.920 --> 00:07:26.672
Ooh, love to hold you

00:07:26.755 --> 00:07:28.674
Ooh, love to kiss you

00:07:28.757 --> 00:07:33.011
Ooh, love, I love it so

00:07:33.887 --> 00:07:35.555
Ooh, love, you're sweeter

00:07:35.639 --> 00:07:37.849
Sweeter than sugar

00:07:37.933 --> 00:07:43.105
Ooh, love, I won't let you go...

00:07:47.401 --> 00:07:48.443
All right, gang.

00:07:48.527 --> 00:07:50.487
I think we have all the clues we need

00:07:50.570 --> 00:07:53.907
to solve the mystery
of the haunted cloning machine.

00:07:53.991 --> 00:07:58.328
Only one person took issue
with the ethical ramifications of cloning

00:07:58.412 --> 00:08:01.248
and also had access to this castle.

00:08:01.331 --> 00:08:03.500
The butler, Dr. Zoidberg!

00:08:03.583 --> 00:08:06.962
Let's see who this so-called butler
really is.

00:08:10.757 --> 00:08:12.175
Oops. Never mind.

00:08:12.259 --> 00:08:13.510
Here, take this.

00:08:21.018 --> 00:08:23.312
Whoa, whoa, whoa...

00:08:25.105 --> 00:08:27.608
May he rest in peace.

00:08:27.691 --> 00:08:29.860
Hey, there's a dragon in this trap!

00:08:29.943 --> 00:08:31.320
Help. Help.

00:08:31.403 --> 00:08:34.448
Let's see who this Dragon Ghost really is.

00:08:36.241 --> 00:08:37.701
George Takei?

00:08:37.784 --> 00:08:38.869
That's right.

00:08:38.952 --> 00:08:40.787
And I would never have
gotten away with it,

00:08:40.871 --> 00:08:42.831
regardless of you meddling kids.

00:08:42.914 --> 00:08:46.501
But, like, that Dragon Ghost
was hovering and translucent.

00:08:46.585 --> 00:08:50.672
Yes. You see, I used the projector
from my kabuki theater.

00:08:50.756 --> 00:08:53.258
But kabuki theaters
don't have a projector.

00:08:53.342 --> 00:08:54.426
Some do.

00:08:54.509 --> 00:08:56.053
It all makes sense.

00:08:56.136 --> 00:08:58.096
He knew that if he scared
the Globetrotters away

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.765
from the big basketball game,

00:08:59.848 --> 00:09:02.809
disappointed fans would flock
to his kabuki theater.

00:09:02.893 --> 00:09:04.269
Of course!

00:09:04.353 --> 00:09:06.980
No, that's not why I did it.

00:09:07.064 --> 00:09:09.107
Then, like, why did you do it?

00:09:09.191 --> 00:09:11.026
I'm mentally ill.

00:09:17.199 --> 00:09:19.660
Thanks for helping solve the mystery.

00:09:19.743 --> 00:09:23.455
After practising against five Larry Birds,
we're ready for anything.

00:09:23.538 --> 00:09:26.166
And now,
introducing the opponents...

00:09:26.249 --> 00:09:28.085
six Larry Birds!

00:09:35.467 --> 00:09:37.928
Bendee-bendee-boo!

00:09:44.851 --> 00:09:47.521
What's all this ruckus?
People live here, you know.

00:09:47.604 --> 00:09:52.401
Mr. President, our children are fat
and dumb, and we blame cartoons.

00:09:52.484 --> 00:09:55.279
It's time to get government
onto our backs.

00:09:55.362 --> 00:09:58.448
We demand you regulate
children's programming

00:09:58.532 --> 00:10:01.994
and force the writers
to shoehorn in helpful lessons.

00:10:02.077 --> 00:10:04.371
Fine, fine. Get off my lawn.

00:10:04.454 --> 00:10:07.541
I'll have Agnew put in a call
to Hollywood.

00:10:14.881 --> 00:10:17.301
All right, let's laugh and learn.

00:10:18.093 --> 00:10:20.345
And now,
the showthat teaches kids

00:10:20.429 --> 00:10:22.264
to eat right and have a good time,

00:10:22.347 --> 00:10:24.474
all whiletolerating others.

00:10:24.558 --> 00:10:27.477
This will shut up those whining hippies.

00:10:27.561 --> 00:10:30.480
Stay tuned
for Purpleberry Pond.

00:10:30.564 --> 00:10:34.067
Purpleberry Pond is fun for young and old

00:10:34.151 --> 00:10:37.279
When healthy juicy purpleberries
fill your bowl

00:10:37.362 --> 00:10:41.742
We all get along and we're happy and merry

00:10:41.825 --> 00:10:45.412
I must get my hands
on those healthy purpleberries!

00:10:45.495 --> 00:10:46.496
Bort.

00:10:46.580 --> 00:10:50.042
Of eating right we are very fond

00:10:50.125 --> 00:10:54.880
When we eat together on Purpleberry Pond

00:11:05.432 --> 00:11:07.601
Good morning, Princess Purpleberry.

00:11:07.684 --> 00:11:09.937
Isn't it a lovely morning?

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:12.940
It's particularly purp-tacular.

00:11:13.023 --> 00:11:15.442
It's pur-practically pur-perfect.

00:11:15.525 --> 00:11:18.779
It's funny how we never get tired
of the word "purple."

00:11:18.862 --> 00:11:19.863
Never.

00:11:19.947 --> 00:11:24.868
And it's all thanks to a balanced diet,
composed of nothing but purpleberries.

00:11:27.871 --> 00:11:31.750
I must get my hands
on those healthy purpleberries!

00:11:31.833 --> 00:11:32.834
Bort.

00:11:34.628 --> 00:11:38.382
Purpleberry Pond
will returnafter these messages.

00:11:38.966 --> 00:11:41.468
Hey, Mickey, you seem kind of down.

00:11:41.551 --> 00:11:44.638
You should try some sugar-blasted
Purpleberry Puffs.

00:11:47.849 --> 00:11:52.020
My sugar-blasted purpleberries
are triple-soaked in maple-flavored syrup

00:11:52.104 --> 00:11:54.481
to start your day with Purple Power.

00:11:54.564 --> 00:11:57.859
And the leftover milk
looks like Purpleberry Pond.

00:11:59.194 --> 00:12:00.195
Ah!

00:12:00.279 --> 00:12:01.863
Purpleberry Puffs
are the sweetest part

00:12:01.947 --> 00:12:03.365
of your complete breakfast,

00:12:03.448 --> 00:12:05.033
along with juice, toast, ham,

00:12:05.117 --> 00:12:09.496
eggs, bacon, milk, cheese, liver, waffles,
and a big horse vitamin.

00:12:09.579 --> 00:12:11.790
And now, back to our show.

00:12:11.873 --> 00:12:13.667
Healthy, healthy, healthy, healthy

00:12:13.750 --> 00:12:15.294
Purpleberries are

00:12:15.377 --> 00:12:19.965
Eat purpleberries and you'll be a star

00:12:20.048 --> 00:12:23.218
Look, a new purp-son
is coming to Purpleberry Pond.

00:12:26.388 --> 00:12:28.682
Announcing Lord Loquat.

00:12:28.765 --> 00:12:31.143
I wonder what shade of purple he'll be.

00:12:35.731 --> 00:12:37.691
Greetings, Princess Purpleberry.

00:12:37.774 --> 00:12:40.736
I am Lord Loquat, your new neighbor.

00:12:40.819 --> 00:12:42.863
You're coming to live here?

00:12:42.946 --> 00:12:44.448
There goes the purple-hood.

00:12:45.324 --> 00:12:48.160
You're different, and I don't like you.

00:12:48.243 --> 00:12:51.580
Wait, it doesn't matter
the color of your berries.

00:12:51.663 --> 00:12:55.626
After all, it takes two colors
to make a rainbow.

00:12:55.709 --> 00:12:58.337
Shucks, I never thought of it that way.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:13:00.047
Sorry, cheddar head.

00:13:00.130 --> 00:13:03.550
Look up high where the rainbow bends

00:13:03.634 --> 00:13:07.512
Orange and purple are the best of friends

00:13:07.596 --> 00:13:11.058
I must get my hands
on those healthy purpleberries!

00:13:11.141 --> 00:13:12.142
Bort.

00:13:12.225 --> 00:13:14.811
And orangeberries.

00:13:16.813 --> 00:13:18.774
We'll be back
after these messages.

00:13:20.901 --> 00:13:24.029
Mom, why is there orange
in my Purpleberry Puffs?

00:13:24.112 --> 00:13:27.282
As an active mom,
I care about these things.

00:13:27.366 --> 00:13:29.743
I'll check the box while you start eating.

00:13:30.702 --> 00:13:35.958
Now my sugar-blasted Purpleberry Puffs
have loquat-flavored orangeberries.

00:13:36.041 --> 00:13:37.668
Two colors?

00:13:37.751 --> 00:13:38.919
Wow!

00:13:41.546 --> 00:13:42.547
Bort.

00:13:42.923 --> 00:13:45.467
It's a small part
of this girl's breakfast.

00:13:55.519 --> 00:13:56.520
Bort?

00:13:56.603 --> 00:14:00.023
I have a plan to get my hands
on those purpleberries

00:14:00.107 --> 00:14:03.151
with new loquat-flavored orangeberries.

00:14:03.235 --> 00:14:07.656
Soon I will have an important part
of a complete breakfast.

00:14:11.285 --> 00:14:12.411
Oh, no.

00:14:12.494 --> 00:14:15.747
The Berry Burglar fired his snowball bomb.

00:14:17.958 --> 00:14:20.711
The snow will destroy
the purpleberry crop.

00:14:22.254 --> 00:14:23.922
Wait, it's not snow.

00:14:24.006 --> 00:14:25.299
It's sugar.

00:14:25.382 --> 00:14:27.259
Yay!

00:14:28.218 --> 00:14:32.139
New sugar-frosted,
sugar-blasted Purpleberry Puffs.

00:14:32.222 --> 00:14:34.182
You can really see the sugar.

00:14:34.266 --> 00:14:38.520
I don't know which I like more,
original or type two.

00:14:41.189 --> 00:14:43.233
And now, back to our show.

00:14:46.028 --> 00:14:50.449
Curses! I didn't get my hands
on those healthy purpleberries.

00:14:50.532 --> 00:14:55.454
But next time, by gosh, I'll get my hands
on those healthy purpleberries.

00:14:55.537 --> 00:14:56.538
Bort.

00:14:57.205 --> 00:14:59.541
Will the Berry Burglar never learn?

00:14:59.625 --> 00:15:02.044
Probably not, but we did.

00:15:02.127 --> 00:15:05.631
We learned that no matter
whether we're purple or orange...

00:15:05.714 --> 00:15:08.508
Or new polkaberry.

00:15:08.592 --> 00:15:11.511
...good nutrition is just a bowl away.

00:15:13.639 --> 00:15:15.349
You know you want to try it

00:15:15.432 --> 00:15:17.309
So tell your mom to buy it

00:15:17.392 --> 00:15:19.686
Buy Purpleberry Puffs cereal.

00:15:19.770 --> 00:15:22.230
Buy! Buy! Buy!

00:15:22.314 --> 00:15:23.315
Bye-bye.

00:15:25.275 --> 00:15:26.860
We'll be back
with more commercials

00:15:26.944 --> 00:15:28.779
after these important messages.

00:15:42.376 --> 00:15:43.877
Go, me!

00:15:45.462 --> 00:15:47.005
They fight for the heck of it

00:15:47.089 --> 00:15:48.674
Because they like to

00:15:48.757 --> 00:15:50.342
Here comes G.I. Zapp

00:15:50.425 --> 00:15:53.095
G.I. Zapp, G.I. Zapp!

00:15:53.637 --> 00:15:56.515
G.I. Zapp
is the code namefor an elite group

00:15:56.598 --> 00:16:00.143
of heavily armed mercenaries,
eager to murder the enemy,

00:16:00.227 --> 00:16:03.313
regardless of the cost in innocent lives.

00:16:07.442 --> 00:16:09.111
Ah, here we go.

00:16:09.194 --> 00:16:12.114
No one can complain
about this patriotic dreck.

00:16:15.325 --> 00:16:16.660
What's that, a rock?

00:16:16.743 --> 00:16:17.995
I hate rocks.

00:16:21.290 --> 00:16:23.583
What do you stupid voters want now?

00:16:23.667 --> 00:16:27.796
What possible objection could you have
to the G.I. Zapp cartoon?

00:16:27.879 --> 00:16:29.506
It's too violent!

00:16:31.049 --> 00:16:33.051
Ooh, very well.

00:16:33.135 --> 00:16:36.096
As leader of the free world,
it is my solemn duty

00:16:36.179 --> 00:16:38.640
to put an end to cartoon violence.

00:16:40.392 --> 00:16:42.394
I'll have to reedit the program.

00:16:42.477 --> 00:16:46.565
Rosemary, have we got any type
of machinery to edit tape?

00:16:46.648 --> 00:16:48.066
Oh, you know we do.

00:16:53.196 --> 00:16:55.866
Time for Dickie to get tricky.

00:16:58.452 --> 00:16:59.870
G.I. Zapp

00:16:59.953 --> 00:17:02.497
G.I. Zapp, G.I. Zapp!

00:17:05.000 --> 00:17:07.878
G.I. Zappis the code name
for an elite group of...

00:17:07.961 --> 00:17:09.838
Patriotic peacekeepers

00:17:09.921 --> 00:17:13.300
who rebuild schools
with their bullet-sucking vacuum tanks.

00:17:13.884 --> 00:17:14.885
That's what they are.

00:17:14.968 --> 00:17:17.846
Today's episode,
"Operation Throat..."

00:17:17.929 --> 00:17:19.097
"Banana Split."

00:17:20.766 --> 00:17:22.643
What the hell kind of plane is that?

00:17:23.894 --> 00:17:25.604
Okay, G.I. Zapps.

00:17:25.687 --> 00:17:28.398
Today's mission is to parachute
into Fort Weaponsworth

00:17:28.482 --> 00:17:30.692
and take back our shrapnel laser,

00:17:30.776 --> 00:17:32.903
which was stolen by our sworn enemy,

00:17:32.986 --> 00:17:35.697
the terrorist group known as ACRONYM.

00:17:36.949 --> 00:17:40.327
ACRONYM.
A Criminal Regiment of Nasty Young Men.

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:43.538
Oh, that's clever.
I'll leave that the way it is.

00:17:50.087 --> 00:17:53.215
I'll show those G.I. Zapps
once and for all

00:17:53.298 --> 00:17:55.092
when I fire this surface-to-air...

00:17:55.175 --> 00:17:56.343
Warning shot.

00:17:56.426 --> 00:17:58.762
Excellent plan, Profestro.

00:17:58.845 --> 00:18:01.348
- That'll blow them straight to h...
- Church.

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:10.107
Sound off as you jump.

00:18:11.525 --> 00:18:12.609
Freezer Burn!

00:18:13.944 --> 00:18:14.945
Nutcracker!

00:18:15.028 --> 00:18:17.698
That's no name for a woman.
Let's just call her Pat.

00:18:17.781 --> 00:18:19.950
- Waterboard!
- Helpful Johnny.

00:18:20.033 --> 00:18:22.077
- Boxcutter!
- Powder Puff.

00:18:22.160 --> 00:18:25.330
- Orphan Crippler!
- Nah, pass.

00:18:29.418 --> 00:18:31.920
- Incoming surface-to-air mi...
- Telegram!

00:18:32.004 --> 00:18:34.506
Pilot, is your parachute packed and ready?

00:18:34.589 --> 00:18:35.632
Yes, sir.

00:18:35.716 --> 00:18:37.342
Good, because I forgot mine.

00:18:41.680 --> 00:18:43.974
Mayday! Mayday! Tell my wife...

00:18:44.057 --> 00:18:45.559
I'll be home for dinner.

00:18:49.896 --> 00:18:51.982
I, uh, landed the plane safely

00:18:52.065 --> 00:18:54.192
next to this naturally occurring fireball.

00:18:54.276 --> 00:18:55.360
At Disneyland.

00:18:56.445 --> 00:18:57.571
Hi, Tinker Bell.

00:19:05.454 --> 00:19:06.663
Ready...

00:19:06.747 --> 00:19:07.873
aim...

00:19:07.956 --> 00:19:09.041
Negotiate.

00:19:19.259 --> 00:19:21.720
Uh, here comes a water balloon.

00:19:23.430 --> 00:19:25.015
That's quite a splash.

00:19:26.600 --> 00:19:28.560
Uh, beam me up, Scotty.

00:19:31.146 --> 00:19:32.731
Yay! I caught it.

00:19:36.318 --> 00:19:38.904
I'm hit. Oh, God, it h...

00:19:38.987 --> 00:19:39.988
Tickles.

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:45.452
Oh, no. Freezer Burn is...

00:19:45.535 --> 00:19:46.536
Sleeping.

00:19:46.620 --> 00:19:48.580
I will avenge him, you heartless...

00:19:48.664 --> 00:19:49.665
Bastards!

00:19:50.165 --> 00:19:51.583
It's okay if I say it.

00:19:54.169 --> 00:19:56.088
Just measuring you for a new hat.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.715
Three, four, cha-cha-cha.

00:20:00.133 --> 00:20:01.426
Find that apple.

00:20:01.510 --> 00:20:02.803
It's down there somewhere.

00:20:15.065 --> 00:20:16.775
That's it, I'm pulling the plug.

00:20:16.858 --> 00:20:18.902
Agnew, cut to the PSA.

00:20:22.155 --> 00:20:23.156
Give me the ball!

00:20:23.240 --> 00:20:24.866
No, give me the ball.

00:20:24.950 --> 00:20:27.494
I know, let's fight for it.

00:20:30.747 --> 00:20:32.332
Now, hold on there, boys.

00:20:32.416 --> 00:20:34.668
Violence never solved anything.

00:20:34.751 --> 00:20:37.087
Then how do we decide who gets the ball?

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.755
Agnew, show them.

00:20:41.842 --> 00:20:44.761
There. How do you like
your stupid ball now?

00:20:50.475 --> 00:20:51.935
Now you know something.

00:20:53.562 --> 00:20:54.563
That concludes

00:20:54.646 --> 00:20:57.399
the Futurama and Friends
Saturday Morning Fun Pit!

00:20:57.482 --> 00:20:59.818
Now stay tuned for six hours of golf.